  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 357 PM EDT Fri Sep 18 2026\n\nThe active weather pattern continues, with additional heavy rainfall \npotential tonight into Sunday morning, possibly lingering into \nMonday. WPC has portions of our area in a moderate risk for \nexcessive rainfall, with the remaining portions of our area in \nslight/marginal risk for excessive rainfall. Opted to issue a \nflash flood watch for portions of IN/MI and a small part of NW \nOH (Van Wert/Paulding Counties, OH). We still remain on the \nnorthern periphery of an upper level ridge/trough to the north, \nwhich keeps us in zonal flow with various shortwaves moving \nthrough. The first arrives late tonight into Saturday, and the \nsecond Saturday night into Sunday morning. The second is \nassociated with a surface low that drifts from IL into our \nforecast area and over to NW OH (or the lower Great Lakes \ndepending on the model). There is considerable uncertainty with \nregards to exact timing, so went broad brush with pops \n(likely/categorical). There is also uncertainty as to where \nexactly the heaviest rain will fall, but for now it looks like \nareas along and north of US 6 will see 2-3 inches of additional \nrainfall, while further south around 1-2\". Locally higher \namounts are possible where training of storms could occur, and \nit's possible the higher totals shift further south. Given \nongoing impacts with river flooding and water over roads (in the\nareas that received 6-10\" of rain this week just south of Fort \nWayne/Allen Co, IN)...decided to err on the side of caution and\nissue the watch. Areas further north saw around 1-3\" (local max\nof around 4\" near our office), but despite these lower amounts \nthis may have primed the pump for flooding if we get the higher \namounts as forecast. \n\nOtherwise, highs will be in the 70s, low 80s through Sunday. There \nis a marginal risk for isolated strong-severe storms Saturday, \nmainly for downburst wind potential (5%) during the day in any \nembedded convection. Low confidence. \n\nAdditional rain chances with periods of thunder through the week, \nbecoming drier towards the Wed-Friday time frame. Cooler, with highs \ndropping into the 60s, and lows in the upper 40s and 50s.",
